do $seed$
declare cid uuid;
begin
  select id into cid from public.courses where slug = 'bib-102';
  insert into public.course_items (course_id, kind, position, title, content) select cid, 'topic', 23, $j$6.3 The Victory of Christ: Faithful and True$j$, $j${"readings": [{"title": "Revelation 12 (King James Version)", "url": "/portal/bible/Revelation/12"}, {"title": "Revelation 19 (King James Version)", "url": "/portal/bible/Revelation/19"}, {"title": "Revelation 20 (King James Version)", "url": "/portal/bible/Revelation/20"}], "body": "Read Revelation 12, Revelation 19 and Revelation 20 in the King James Version. Then read this lesson.\n\nThe middle chapters of Revelation describe a great struggle between good and evil, using symbols that the first readers understood. The message of these chapters is that Jesus wins. In Revelation 12:11 John wrote that believers overcame by the blood of the Lamb, by the word of their testimony, and because they loved not their lives unto the death. In chapter 19 John saw heaven opened and Christ riding a white horse. He is called Faithful and True, His name is The Word of God, and He has written on Him the name KING OF KINGS, AND LORD OF LORDS. In chapter 20 John saw the great white throne, where the dead are judged and the book of life is opened. Christians have studied the details of these chapters in different ways, but all agree that Christ will return in victory and that every person will stand before God.\n\nKey words: overcame, testimony, Faithful and True, King of kings, judgment.\n\nYour task: (1) Tell how Revelation 12:11 says believers overcame. (2) Write Revelation 19:16 in your own words. (3) Explain what John saw at the great white throne in Revelation 20.\n\nCourse area: Bible elective. Scripture is read from the King James Version.", "video": "", "presenter": "Dr. Alex L. Jenkins Sr.", "standards": "Bible elective", "script": "Today we look at the chapters of Revelation that show the final victory of Christ. This part of the book uses vivid symbols, such as beasts, dragons and horsemen. Christians through the centuries have studied these symbols and sometimes explained them in different ways. As students, we will focus on what is clear and what all believers agree on: Jesus wins, and every person will stand before God.\n\nThe book of Revelation was written to encourage believers who were suffering. Many of them were being persecuted by the Roman Empire. John wanted them to know how this struggle will end. In chapter 12 he showed how God's people can overcome. Revelation 12:11 says, And they overcame him by the blood of the Lamb, and by the word of their testimony; and they loved not their lives unto the death. Believers overcome by the blood of Jesus, by their testimony, and by their willingness to stay faithful, even in hard times.\n\nChapter 19 gives us a picture of the return of Christ. Revelation 19:11 says, And I saw heaven opened, and behold a white horse; and he that sat upon him was called Faithful and True, and in righteousness he doth judge and make war. The name Faithful and True tells us that Jesus always keeps His word. Verse 12 says, His eyes were as a flame of fire, and on his head were many crowns; and he had a name written, that no man knew, but he himself. Verse 13 says, And he was clothed with a vesture dipped in blood: and his name is called The Word of God. This links us back to the Gospel of John, which began by calling Jesus the Word. Verse 16 gives His title. And he hath on his vesture and on his thigh a name written, KING OF KINGS, AND LORD OF LORDS. No ruler, empire or power is greater than Jesus.\n\nChapter 20 describes a solemn moment. Revelation 20:11 says, And I saw a great white throne, and him that sat on it, from whose face the earth and the heaven fled away; and there was found no place for them. Verse 12 says, And I saw the dead, small and great, stand before God; and the books were opened: and another book was opened, which is the book of life: and the dead were judged out of those things which were written in the books, according to their works. Everyone, great and small, will stand before God. Verse 15 says, And whosoever was not found written in the book of life was cast into the lake of fire. This is a serious truth, and it is the reason the gospel must be shared. Those who trust in Jesus have their names written in the book of life.\n\nYour task is to tell how Revelation 12:11 says believers overcame, write Revelation 19:16 in your own words, and explain what John saw at the great white throne. Then take the four question check.\n\nJesus is Faithful and True, and He is King of kings. Excellence, Faith, Purpose. I will see you in the next lesson."}$j$::jsonb where not exists (select 1 from public.course_items where course_id = cid and kind = 'topic' and title = $j$6.3 The Victory of Christ: Faithful and True$j$);
end
$seed$;
